{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Wood Gatherer: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja7'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 7 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Apaṇṇakavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sure Bet </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>7. Kaṭṭhahārijātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Wood Gatherer: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Putto tyāhaṁ mahārāja, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I am your son, Great King! </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>tvaṁ maṁ posa janādhipa; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Provide for me, ruler of the people. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Aññepi devo poseti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The king provides for others, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kiñca devo sakaṁ pajan”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>what then of his own offspring? </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Kaṭṭhahārijātakaṁ sattamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
